 *Not required for AWS Bedrock - use standard AWS credential chain (IAM roles, environment variables, ~/.aws/credentials)
 
+### IdP-Authenticated Endpoints (OAuth2 Client-Credentials)
+
+Some enterprise embedding endpoints are OpenAI-compatible on the wire but are gated by a
+short-lived access token (typically a ~60 minute JWT) issued by an identity provider. With
+the static `EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY`, such endpoints start returning 401 after one token
+lifetime. Enable IdP mode to obtain and refresh the bearer automatically:
+
+```bash
+# In .env
+EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=litellm
+EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_NAME=openai/text-embedding-3-small
+EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_DIMENSIONS=1536
+EMBEDDINGS_IDP_ENABLED=true
+EMBEDDINGS_IDP_TOKEN_URL=https://idp.example.com/oauth2/token
+EMBEDDINGS_IDP_CLIENT_ID=embeddings-client
+EMBEDDINGS_IDP_CLIENT_SECRET=your-idp-client-secret
+# Optional:
+#EMBEDDINGS_IDP_SCOPE=embeddings.read
+#EMBEDDINGS_IDP_REFRESH_BUFFER_SECONDS=60
+```
+
+Behaviour:
+
+- Each embedding call sends a freshly obtained `Authorization: Bearer` token (OAuth2
+  client-credentials grant) via LiteLLM's per-call `api_key`; the static `EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY`
+  is not used and is not pushed into provider environment variables in this mode.
+- The token is cached in memory and refreshed automatically before it expires
+  (`EMBEDDINGS_IDP_REFRESH_BUFFER_SECONDS` early; keep at least 60 seconds so clock skew
+  cannot serve an already-expired token).
+- Startup fails fast with a clear error if IdP mode is enabled but the token URL, client
+  ID, or client secret is missing.
+- The client secret is never logged and is masked in the config UI.
+- All IdP settings default to unset/disabled: with them unset, existing providers behave
+  exactly as before.
+
+**Dimension / re-index caveat:** switching to an IdP-gated endpoint usually means switching
+embedding models, and a different model usually produces a different vector dimension. The
+collection/index name embeds the configured `EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_DIMENSIONS`, so changing the
+model requires re-indexing existing content (or accepting degraded hybrid-search quality).
+See the [switching embedding models FAQ](faq/switching-embedding-models.md).
+
 ### Terraform Configuration
 
 For AWS ECS deployments, configure embeddings in your `terraform.tfvars`:
