+| IdP scope | `EMBEDDINGS_IDP_SCOPE` | `embeddings_idp_scope` | `extraEnv` | Optional space-separated OAuth2 scope. |
+| IdP refresh buffer | `EMBEDDINGS_IDP_REFRESH_BUFFER_SECONDS` | `embeddings_idp_refresh_buffer_seconds` | `extraEnv` | Refresh the bearer this many seconds before expiry. Default `60`; at least 60 recommended. |
+
+For the IdP parameters on Helm, the registry chart carries `EMBEDDINGS_*` variables through
+the generic `extraEnv` / `extraEnvFrom` mechanism (validated against the chart's reserved
+names). Example for the registry subchart:
+
+```yaml
+extraEnv:
+  - name: EMBEDDINGS_IDP_ENABLED
+    value: "true"
+  - name: EMBEDDINGS_IDP_TOKEN_URL
+    value: "https://idp.example.com/oauth2/token"
+  - name: EMBEDDINGS_IDP_CLIENT_ID
+    value: "embeddings-client"
+extraEnvFrom:
+  - secretRef:
+      name: embeddings-idp   # must expose EMBEDDINGS_IDP_CLIENT_SECRET
+```
+
+When `EMBEDDINGS_IDP_ENABLED=true`, IdP mode replaces the static API key on the embeddings
+path: each call sends a freshly obtained `Authorization: Bearer` token (OAuth2
+client-credentials grant), refreshed automatically before it expires. Startup fails fast if
+the token URL, client ID, or client secret is missing. Note the dimension caveat: an
+IdP-gated endpoint usually implies a different embedding model and dimension, so existing
+vectors must be re-indexed or search quality degrades — see
+`docs/faq/switching-embedding-models.md`.
 
